china was the fifth nation in history to  become a nuclear power when it detonated  an atomic weapon in 1964. yet given the  fact that china hadn't fully  industrialized yet was internationally  isolated and its economy was on the  verge of collapse how did it manage to  do it how did china build a nuclear  weapons program so as of the 1950s china  had just finished a long and brutal  civil war which had been preceded by  world war ii the civil war had seen  mao's communists victorious with the  defeated chiang kai-shek's government  fleeing to taiwan when tensions between  the mainland and taiwan flared up in the  mid-50s the united states got involved  meaning mao was stuck to china's  leadership this meant that obtaining the  bomb was the best way to avoid a  humiliating repeat and fortunately mao  had a nuclear ally to the north the ussr  which was happy to help china require  nuclear weapons because china having  them had little effect on the ussr but  it sure did make the lives of america  and its allies in the region a lot  harder so off they went now the ussr had  tested its first weapon five years  earlier than this and so had a lot of  expertise by this point and the soviet  leader nikita khrushchev saw this  expertise as something that he could  leverage against china to keep it under  control you see khrushchev and the rest  of the soviet leadership were starting  to move away from that whole stalinism  bit of their history and given that mao  was a fan they saw a potential conflict  on the horizon and so what they did was  make sure that soviet scientists were in  control of the project and that without  them china wouldn't be able to complete  it which is why when mao denounced  khrushchev as a lame fake communist who  was too nice to the west the soviets  withdrew from the program taking both  know-how and important components with  them this left the chinese not knowing  how to proceed safely but mao wasn't  interested in safety mao was interested  in proceeding now it won't shock you to  know that trying to fumble your way  through building nuclear weapons using  what the soviets left behind and hoping  for the best was not a great plan and as  a result there were numerous setbacks  the death e turns out this stuff is kind  of dangerous style of setbacks  eventually the chinese government  accepted that you can't just demand that  science be achieved and it allowed the  program more space and within five years  of this the scientists involved had  cracked it and china was ready to test  its own bomb which it did in late 1964  much to the annoyance of the already  existing western nuclear powers who  previously only had to worry about the  soviets the americans were particularly  worried about another country building  massive amounts of weapons that they'd  have to match warhead for warhead but  the chinese opted to not go down that  route instead the chinese military  pushed for a strategy of making any  nuclear war with china cost too much  which is the strategy that china as the  world's fifth nuclear power still uses  to this day i hope you enjoyed this  episode and thank you for watching with  a special thanks to my patrons james  bissonette mr wolfe kelly moneymaker  skye chappelle jerry lamdin jordan  longley adam stalter corso wolf gareth  turner marvin castell why in hockey  captain cydog spencer lightfoot boogerly  wiggly matthew shipley maggie paxkowski  aaron the white robert wetzel marcus  asner anthony beckett alex schwinn the  muk whopper gustav swan coppertone  spinning three plates mo winston cayward  charles the first ben evanson and  scottish trekkie
 

